description:
Row-major dense `FieldMatrix<F: FiniteField>` type built on `FieldVec<F>`. Delivers the full `BitMatrix`-parity public surface plus the Armadillo-shape convenience operations listed in `dev/plans/armadillo_ux_mapping.md`. Introduces the `MatrixLike<Elem>` shared trait and has `BitMatrix` (bool) and `FieldMatrix<F>` (F) both implement it.

## API surface (must match `BitMatrix` method-for-method where applicable)

```rust
pub struct FieldMatrix<F: FiniteField> {
    rows: usize,
    cols: usize,
    data: FieldVec<F>, // row-major, stride = cols
}

impl<F: FiniteField> FieldMatrix<F> {
    // Constructors (parity with BitMatrix where names exist)
    pub fn new(rows: usize, cols: usize, fill: F) -> Self;
    pub fn from_rows(rows: Vec<FieldVec<F>>) -> Self;
    pub fn with_capacity(rows: usize, cols: usize) -> Self;

    // Shape
    pub fn rows(&self) -> usize;
    pub fn cols(&self) -> usize;
    pub fn shape(&self) -> (usize, usize);
    pub fn is_square(&self) -> bool;
    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool;

    // Element access
    pub fn get(&self, r: usize, c: usize) -> F;
    pub fn set(&mut self, r: usize, c: usize, v: F);
    pub fn get_unchecked(&self, r: usize, c: usize) -> F;

    // Row/col access
    pub fn row(&self, i: usize) -> &[F];
    pub fn row_mut(&mut self, i: usize) -> &mut [F];
    pub fn col(&self, j: usize) -> ColView<'_, F>;
    pub fn col_iter(&self, j: usize) -> impl Iterator<Item = &F>;

    // Views (Armadillo-style submat)
    pub fn submat(&self, rows: impl RangeBounds<usize>, cols: impl RangeBounds<usize>) -> MatView<'_, F>;
    pub fn submat_mut(&mut self, rows: impl RangeBounds<usize>, cols: impl RangeBounds<usize>) -> MatViewMut<'_, F>;
    pub fn row_range(&self, rows: impl RangeBounds<usize>) -> MatView<'_, F>;
    pub fn col_range(&self, cols: impl RangeBounds<usize>) -> MatView<'_, F>;

    // Row operations (needed by Gaussian elimination / PLE)
    pub fn swap_rows(&mut self, r1: usize, r2: usize);
    pub fn scale_row(&mut self, row: usize, factor: F);
    pub fn axpy_row(&mut self, dst: usize, src: usize, factor: F); // parity with BitMatrix::row_xor
    pub fn find_pivot_row(&self, col: usize, start_row: usize) -> Option<usize>;

    // Derived
    pub fn transpose(&self) -> Self;
    pub fn t(&self) -> Transposed<&Self>;           // lazy proxy (design in cdcebf6a)
    pub fn diag(&self) -> FieldVec<F>;
    pub fn trace(&self) -> F;
    pub fn is_symmetric(&self) -> bool;

    // Conversion
    pub fn to_sparse(&self) -> SparseFieldMatrix<F>; // mirrors BitMatrix::to_sparse, from story 8a90882e
    pub fn matvec(&self, x: &FieldVec<F>) -> FieldVec<F>;
    pub fn matvec_transpose(&self, x: &FieldVec<F>) -> FieldVec<F>;
}

impl<F: ConstField> FieldMatrix<F> {
    pub fn zeros(rows: usize, cols: usize) -> Self;
    pub fn ones(rows: usize, cols: usize) -> Self;
    pub fn identity(n: usize) -> Self;
    pub fn random<R: Rng>(rows: usize, cols: usize, rng: &mut R) -> Self;
    pub fn random_seeded(rows: usize, cols: usize, seed: u64) -> Self;
}

// Operator overloads — all four owned/ref combos for Mul/Add/Sub (per BitMatrix precedent).
// Scalar multiplication F * M and M * F.
// Neg for -A.
// Index<(usize, usize)> for A[(i, j)].
// Display (styled consistently with BitMatrix::Display).
```

## `MatrixLike<Elem>` shared trait

New module `crates/gf2-core/src/matrix_like.rs`:

```rust
pub trait MatrixLike<Elem> {
    fn rows(&self) -> usize;
    fn cols(&self) -> usize;
    fn get(&self, row: usize, col: usize) -> Elem;
    fn set(&mut self, row: usize, col: usize, v: Elem);
    fn swap_rows(&mut self, r1: usize, r2: usize);
    fn transpose(&self) -> Self where Self: Sized;
    fn shape(&self) -> (usize, usize) { (self.rows(), self.cols()) }
    fn is_square(&self) -> bool { self.rows() == self.cols() }
    fn is_empty(&self) -> bool { self.rows() == 0 || self.cols() == 0 }
}
```

`BitMatrix` gains a trivial `MatrixLike<bool>` impl in `matrix.rs`. No behavioral change to existing `BitMatrix` users. `FieldMatrix<F>` implements `MatrixLike<F>` in `field/matrix.rs`. `MatView<'_, F>` / `MatViewMut<'_, F>` also implement it (read-only variant for `MatView`), so algorithms written against `MatrixLike` can recurse into submatrix views without copying.

## Location

- `crates/gf2-core/src/field/matrix.rs` — `FieldMatrix<F>`, `MatView`, `MatViewMut`, `ColView`
- `crates/gf2-core/src/matrix_like.rs` — `MatrixLike<Elem>` trait
- `crates/gf2-core/src/matrix.rs` — add `MatrixLike<bool>` impl for `BitMatrix` (non-invasive)

## Non-goals

- Operator expression-template proxy types — those are designed in `cdcebf6a` and implemented in `d48a3cfd`.
- Sparse conversion body — `to_sparse` signature is declared here but implementation is in `8a90882e`.
- Matrix multiplication — algorithmic body lives in `d48a3cfd`; only the `Mul` trait shell and signature land here.

## Known limitations (user-approved 2026-04-23)

- **Zero-inner-dimension products on runtime-context fields.** The operations `gemm`, `matvec`, and `matvec_transpose` are mathematically total over any field: for shapes like `(m × 0) * (0 × n)` the result is the m×n zero matrix. For `F: ConstField` (all `Fp<P>`, `QuadraticExt`, `CubicExt`, `GoldilocksFp`, `Gf2mWide`) these operations are implemented totally — `F::zero()` is a static function and no witness is needed.

  For `F: FiniteField` that is **not** `ConstField` (currently only `Gf2mElement`, which carries its polynomial field context inside each element), a `(m × 0)` or `(0 × n)` operand has zero elements and therefore no witness is available to construct a zero of the correct field. In this narrow degenerate corner the implementation panics with a documented message. This limitation is acceptable because:
  1. All downstream call sites in this epic that involve factorizations (PLE `c3f8c1cb`, inv/solve `ae1d1e88`, charpoly `e47231cd`) are parameterized over `F: ConstField` in practice, so the panic is unreachable in normal use.
  2. `FiniteField::zero_hint() -> Option<Self>` is exposed so callers who need a zero for a runtime-context field can obtain one when the field happens to expose a static default, and the corner stays an honest partial function rather than silent wrong-answer behavior.
  3. The mechanical test `test_gemm_panics_for_zero_inner_without_const_zero` locks the panic behavior so downstream stories can build on a documented contract.

## Success criteria

- [hard] Every `BitMatrix` method listed above has a signature-parity counterpart on `FieldMatrix<F>` or a clear justification in the PR description for why it does not apply.
- [hard] `MatrixLike<Elem>` trait exists and is implemented by `BitMatrix`, `FieldMatrix<F>`, and at least `MatView<'_, F>`.
- [hard] `BitMatrix`'s public behavior is unchanged (existing tests still pass without modification).
- [hard] Every public item has a doc comment with `# Examples` (doctest-compiled) and `# Complexity` for non-trivial operations.
- [hard] Display output for `FieldMatrix<F>` follows `BitMatrix::Display`'s alignment conventions.
- [hard] Criterion micro-benchmarks exist for `FieldMatrix::zeros`, `identity`, `transpose`, `row`/`col` access at representative sizes.
- [hard] `cargo test --workspace --all-features --release --profile ci` + `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` + `cargo fmt --all -- --check` all pass.
- [hard] `gemm`, `matvec`, `matvec_transpose` are total over `F: ConstField`; over `F: FiniteField` they may panic with a documented message in the zero-inner-dimension corner (see "Known limitations"). Tests lock the panic behavior for `Gf2mElement`.

## Dependencies

- GF(p^m) foundation (`e095a100`) — DONE.
- Expression-template design (`cdcebf6a`) — **informational only**; operator overload signatures land here but the proxy types are implemented in `d48a3cfd`. This story is not blocked by cdcebf6a but is dispatched in parallel wave.

